{"id":"mahabharata-5-081","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":81,"title":"एकाशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 81 · Krishna sets out for Hastinapura","summary":{"en":"Arjuna asks Krishna to bring about peace if possible, and Krishna sets out at dawn in his chariot with Satyaki. Yudhishthira sends greetings to Kunti, recalling her sufferings, and on the way Krishna meets Parashurama, Kanva, Narada and other sages, who say they will come to the Kuru assembly to hear him.","kn":"ಸಾಧ್ಯವಾದರೆ ಶಾಂತಿ ತರಬೇಕೆಂದು ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಬೆಳಗ್ಗೆ ರಥದಲ್ಲಿ ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಕುಂತಿಯ ಕಷ್ಟಗಳನ್ನು ನೆನೆದು ಅವಳಿಗೆ ನಮಸ್ಕಾರ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದಾರಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಪರಶುರಾಮ, ಕಣ್ವ, ನಾರದ ಮೊದಲಾದ ಋಷಿಗಳನ್ನು ಭೇಟಿಯಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅವರು ಕುರುಸಭೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಅವನ ಮಾತು ಕೇಳಲು ಬರುವೆವೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन श्रीकृष्ण से सम्भव हो तो शान्ति कराने को कहते हैं, और श्रीकृष्ण भोर में सात्यकि के साथ रथ पर निकलते हैं। युधिष्ठिर कुन्ती के कष्टों को याद कर उन्हें प्रणाम भेजते हैं, और मार्ग में श्रीकृष्ण परशुराम, कण्व, नारद और अन्य ऋषियों से मिलते हैं, जो कहते हैं कि वे कुरु सभा में उनकी बात सुनने आएँगे।","te":"వీలైతే శాంతి సాధించమని అర్జునుడు శ్రీకృష్ణుని కోరతాడు; శ్రీకృష్ణుడు సాత్యకితో తెల్లవారుజామున రథంపై బయలుదేరుతాడు. యుధిష్ఠిరుడు కుంతి కష్టాలను గుర్తుచేసుకొని ఆమెకు నమస్కారాలు పంపుతాడు; దారిలో శ్రీకృష్ణుడు పరశురాముడు, కణ్వుడు, నారదుడు మొదలైన ఋషులను కలుస్తాడు, వారు కురుసభలో ఆయన మాట వినడానికి వస్తామంటారు.","ta":"இயன்றால் அமைதியைக் கொணருமாறு அர்ஜுனன் கேட்க, ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் விடியலில் ஸாத்யகியுடன் தேரில் புறப்படுகிறார். யுதிஷ்டிரர் குந்தியின் துன்பங்களை நினைவுகூர்ந்து அவளுக்கு வணக்கம் அனுப்புகிறார்; வழியில் ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் பரஶுராமர், கண்வர், நாரதர் முதலிய முனிவர்களைச் சந்திக்க, அவர் பேச்சைக் கேட்கக் குரு சபைக்கு வருவதாக அவர்கள் சொல்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"സാധ്യമെങ്കിൽ സമാധാനമുണ്ടാക്കണമെന്ന് അർജുനൻ കൃഷ്ണനോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു; കൃഷ്ണൻ സാത്യകിയോടൊപ്പം തേരിൽ പുലർച്ചെ പുറപ്പെടുന്നു. കുന്തിയെ സന്ദേശമയച്ച് വണങ്ങാൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പറയുന്നു; അവരുടെ കഷ്ടപ്പാടുകൾ അദ്ദേഹം ഓർമ്മിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. വഴിയിൽ പരശുരാമൻ, കണ്വൻ, നാരദൻ തുടങ്ങിയ മുനിമാരെ കാണുന്ന കൃഷ്ണനോട് അവർ കൗരവസഭയിൽ കേൾക്കാൻ എത്താമെന്ന് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.81; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कुरूणामद्य सर्वेषां भवान्सुहृदनुत्तमः ।\nसंबन्धी दयितो नित्यमुभयोः पक्षयोरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, you are today the best friend of all the Kurus, a dear kinsman always to both sides."}},{"n":2,"text":"पाण्डवैर्धार्तराष्ट्राणां प्रतिपाद्यमनामयम् ।\nसमर्थः प्रशमं चैषां कर्तुं त्वमसि केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"You can bring about peace between the Pandavas and the Dhartarashtras, so that both are free from harm, Keshava."}},{"n":3,"text":"त्वमितः पुण्डरीकाक्ष सुयोधनममर्षणम् ।\nशान्त्यर्थं भारतं ब्रूया यत्तद्वाच्यममित्रहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lotus-eyed destroyer of enemies, go from here and tell the angry Duryodhana, the Bharata, whatever should be said for peace."}},{"n":4,"text":"त्वया धर्मार्थयुक्तं चेदुक्तं शिवमनामयम् ।\nहितं नादास्यते बालो दिष्टस्य वशमेष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, spoken by you, beneficial and flawless words full of dharma and profit are not accepted by that childish man, he will fall under the power of fate."}},{"text":"भगवानुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The Blessed Lord said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"धर्म्यमस्मद्धितं चैव कुरूणां यदनामयम् ।\nएष यास्यामि राजानं धृतराष्ट्रमभीप्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is in accord with dharma, good for us and harmless to the Kurus, I shall go to King Dhritarashtra with that aim."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"ततो व्यपेते तमसि सूर्ये विमल उद्गते ।\nमैत्रे मुहूर्ते संप्राप्ते मृद्वर्चिषि दिवाकरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, when darkness had gone and the clear sun had risen, at the Maitra hour, when the sun's rays were soft,"}},{"n":7,"text":"कौमुदे मासि रेवत्यां शरदन्ते हिमागमे ।\nस्फीतसस्यसुखे काले कल्यः सत्त्ववतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"in the month of Kaumuda, under the star Revati, at autumn's end as winter came, in a season of rich crops and ease, the best of the strong stood ready."}},{"n":8,"text":"मङ्गल्याः पुण्यनिर्घोषा वाचः शृण्वंश्च सूनृताः ।\nब्राह्मणानां प्रतीतानामृषीणामिव वासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing auspicious, sacred words and truthful speech from trusted brahmanas, as Indra hears from sages,"}},{"n":9,"text":"कृत्वा पौर्वाह्णिकं कृत्यं स्नातः शुचिरलंकृतः ।\nउपतस्थे विवस्वन्तं पावकं च जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Janardana performed his morning rites, bathed, purified and adorned, and worshiped the sun and the fire."}},{"n":10,"text":"ऋषभं पृष्ठ आलभ्य ब्राह्मणानभिवाद्य च ।\nअग्निं प्रदक्षिणं कृत्वा पश्यन्कल्याणमग्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He touched the back of a bull, saluted the brahmanas, circled the fire to the right, and looked on the auspicious signs before him."}},{"n":11,"text":"तत्प्रतिज्ञाय वचनं पाण्डवस्य जनार्दनः ।\nशिनेर्नप्तारमासीनमभ्यभाषत सात्यकिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having promised Pandava's request, Janardana spoke to Satyaki, Shini's grandson, who sat nearby."}},{"n":12,"text":"रथ आरोप्यतां शङ्खश्चक्रं च गदया सह ।\nउपासङ्गाश्च शक्त्यश्च सर्वप्रहरणानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Have the conch, the discus and the mace placed on the chariot, with quivers, spears and all weapons."}},{"n":13,"text":"दुर्योधनो हि दुष्टात्मा कर्णश्च सहसौबलः ।\nन च शत्रुरवज्ञेयः प्राकृतोऽपि बलीयसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Duryodhana is evil-minded, and so are Karna and Saubala; and an enemy, even a common one, should never be despised by someone stronger."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततस्तन्मतमाज्ञाय केशवस्य पुरःसराः ।\nप्रसस्रुर्योजयिष्यन्तो रथं चक्रगदाभृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, understanding Keshava's wish, his attendants went ahead to harness the chariot for the bearer of discus and mace."}},{"n":15,"text":"तं दीप्तमिव कालाग्निमाकाशगमिवाध्वगम् ।\nचन्द्रसूर्यप्रकाशाभ्यां चक्राभ्यां समलंकृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That chariot gleamed like the fire of doom, moved as if through the sky, and was adorned with two wheels bright as moon and sun."}},{"n":16,"text":"अर्धचन्द्रैश्च चन्द्रैश्च मत्स्यैः समृगपक्षिभिः ।\nपुष्पैश्च विविधैश्चित्रं मणिरत्नैश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was decorated with half-moons and full moons, with fish, beasts and birds, with many flowers, and with jewels and gems all over."}},{"n":17,"text":"तरुणादित्यसंकाशं बृहन्तं चारुदर्शनम् ।\nमणिहेमविचित्राङ्गं सुध्वजं सुपताकिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was large and lovely to see, like the young sun, its parts variegated with gems and gold, with a fine banner and flags."}},{"n":18,"text":"सूपस्करमनाधृष्यं वैयाघ्रपरिवारणम् ।\nयशोघ्नं प्रत्यमित्राणां यदूनां नन्दिवर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fully equipped, unassailable, ringed with tiger skins, it dimmed the fame of enemies and increased the joy of the Yadavas."}},{"n":19,"text":"वाजिभिः सैन्यसुग्रीवमेघपुष्पबलाहकैः ।\nस्नातैः संपादयां चक्रुः संपन्नैः सर्वसंपदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"They yoked to it the horses Shaibya, Sugriva, Meghapushpa and Balahaka, bathed and rich in every excellence."}},{"n":20,"text":"महिमानं तु कृष्णस्य भूय एवाभिवर्धयन् ।\nसुघोषः पतगेन्द्रेण ध्वजेन युयुजे रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Further to enhance Krishna's greatness, the chariot named Sughosha was fitted with the banner of Garuda, lord of birds."}},{"n":21,"text":"तं मेरुशिखरप्रख्यं मेघदुन्दुभिनिस्वनम् ।\nआरुरोह रथं शौरिर्विमानमिव पुण्यकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shauri mounted it, like a doer of merit boarding a heavenly car; it looked like the peak of Meru and roared like a thundercloud drum."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततः सात्यकिमारोप्य प्रययौ पुरुषोत्तमः ।\nपृथिवीं चान्तरिक्षं च रथघोषेण नादयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having Satyaki ascend, the best of men set out, filling earth and sky with the chariot's rumble."}},{"n":23,"text":"व्यपोढाभ्रघनः कालः क्षणेन समपद्यत ।\nशिवश्चानुववौ वायुः प्रशान्तमभवद्रजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In an instant the time became clear, the clouds gone; a gentle wind blew and the dust settled."}},{"n":24,"text":"प्रदक्षिणानुलोमाश्च मङ्गल्या मृगपक्षिणः ।\nप्रयाणे वासुदेवस्य बभूवुरनुयायिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Auspicious beasts and birds, moving to the right and in a favorable way, followed Vasudeva on his journey."}},{"n":25,"text":"मङ्गल्यार्थपदैः शब्दैरन्ववर्तन्त सर्वशः ।\nसारसाः शतपत्राश्च हंसाश्च मधुसूदनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cranes, shatapatra birds and swans followed Madhusudana on every side with auspicious, meaningful cries."}},{"n":26,"text":"मन्त्राहुतिमहाहोमैर्हूयमानश्च पावकः ।\nप्रदक्षिणशिखो भूत्वा विधूमः समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sacrificial fire fed with mantras and offerings turned its flames to the right and burned without smoke."}},{"n":27,"text":"वसिष्ठो वामदेवश्च भूरिद्युम्नो गयः क्रथः ।\nशुक्रनारदवाल्मीका मरुतः कुशिको भृगुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasishtha, Vamadeva, Bhuridyumna, Gaya, Kratha, Shukra, Narada, Valmiki, the Maruts, Kushika and Bhrigu,"}},{"n":28,"text":"ब्रह्मदेवर्षयश्चैव कृष्णं यदुसुखावहम् ।\nप्रदक्षिणमवर्तन्त सहिता वासवानुजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Brahmarshis and Devarshis all together circled around Krishna, younger brother of Indra, bringer of joy to the Yadavas."}},{"n":29,"text":"एवमेतैर्महाभागैर्महर्षिगणसाधुभिः ।\nपूजितः प्रययौ कृष्णः कुरूणां सदनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honored thus by these great and noble companies of sages, Krishna went toward the home of the Kurus."}},{"n":30,"text":"तं प्रयान्तमनुप्रायात्कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nभीमसेनार्जुनौ चोभौ माद्रीपुत्रौ च पाण्डवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he went, Yudhishthira son of Kunti followed him, with Bhimasena and Arjuna and the two sons of Madri."}},{"n":31,"text":"चेकितानश्च विक्रान्तो धृष्टकेतुश्च चेदिपः ।\nद्रुपदः काशिराजश्च शिखण्डी च महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Also the valiant Chekitana, Dhrishtaketu lord of Chedi, Drupada, the king of Kashi, and the great warrior Shikhandi,"}},{"n":32,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नः सपुत्रश्च विराटः केकयैः सह ।\nसंसाधनार्थं प्रययुः क्षत्रियाः क्षत्रियर्षभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna with his sons, and Virata with the Kekayas: these kshatriyas went with the bull of kshatriyas to help him on his way."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततोऽनुव्रज्य गोविन्दं धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nराज्ञां सकाशे द्युतिमानुवाचेदं वचस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, accompanying Govinda, the brilliant Yudhishthira, king of dharma, spoke these words in the presence of the kings."}},{"n":34,"text":"यो नैव कामान्न भयान्न लोभान्नार्थकारणात् ।\nअन्यायमनुवर्तेत स्थिरबुद्धिरलोलुपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keshava does not follow injustice from desire, fear, greed or gain; he is steady-minded and free from covetousness."}},{"n":35,"text":"धर्मज्ञो धृतिमान्प्राज्ञः सर्वभूतेषु केशवः ।\nईश्वरः सर्वभूतानां देवदेवः प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He knows dharma, is resolute and wise toward all beings, a lord of all creatures, god of gods and full of majesty."}},{"n":36,"text":"तं सर्वगुणसंपन्नं श्रीवत्सकृतलक्षणम् ।\nसंपरिष्वज्य कौन्तेयः संदेष्टुमुपचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Embracing him, endowed with every virtue and marked with the Shrivatsa, the son of Kunti began to give him messages."}},{"n":37,"text":"या सा बाल्यात्प्रभृत्यस्मान्पर्यवर्धयताबला ।\nउपवासतपःशीला सदा स्वस्त्ययने रता ॥","meaning":{"en":"She who raised us from childhood, a woman without protector, devoted to fasting and austerity, always intent on blessings,"}},{"n":38,"text":"देवतातिथिपूजासु गुरुशुश्रूषणे रता ।\nवत्सला प्रियपुत्रा च प्रियास्माकं जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"devoted to worship of the gods and guests and to serving elders, loving, fond of her sons, dear to us, Janardana,"}},{"n":39,"text":"सुयोधनभयाद्या नोऽत्रायतामित्रकर्शन ।\nमहतो मृत्युसंबाधादुत्तरन्नौरिवार्णवात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"she who saved us from Suyodhana's menace, destroyer of foes, as a boat carries across the ocean from great peril of death:"}},{"n":40,"text":"अस्मत्कृते च सततं यया दुःखानि माधव ।\nअनुभूतान्यदुःखार्हा तां स्म पृच्छेरनामयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"ask after her welfare, she who always bore sorrow for our sake though she did not deserve sorrow."}},{"n":41,"text":"भृशमाश्वासयेश्चैनां पुत्रशोकपरिप्लुताम् ।\nअभिवाद्य स्वजेथाश्च पाण्डवान्परिकीर्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Comfort her greatly, she who is steeped in grief for her sons; salute her and embrace her, speaking of the Pandavas."}},{"n":42,"text":"ऊढात्प्रभृति दुःखानि श्वशुराणामरिंदम ।\nनिकारानतदर्हा च पश्यन्ती दुःखमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since her marriage she has known sorrows from her in-laws, slayer of foes, and, undeserving, she suffers seeing the wrongs done."}},{"n":43,"text":"अपि जातु स कालः स्यात्कृष्ण दुःखविपर्ययः ।\nयदहं मातरं क्लिष्टां सुखे दध्यामरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, might there ever come a time of reversal from sorrow, when I could set my afflicted mother in happiness?"}},{"n":44,"text":"प्रव्रजन्तोऽन्वधावत्सा कृपणा पुत्रगृद्धिनी ।\nरुदतीमपहायैनामुपगच्छाम यद्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When we went to the forest she, wretched and clinging to her sons, ran after us; we left her weeping and went on."}},{"n":45,"text":"न नूनं म्रियते दुःखैः सा चेज्जीवति केशव ।\nतथा पुत्राधिभिर्गाढमार्ता ह्यानर्तसत्कृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely she does not die of sorrow if she still lives, Keshava, so deeply pained by anxiety for her sons, though honored among the Anartas."}},{"n":46,"text":"अभिवाद्या तु सा कृष्ण त्वया मद्वचनाद्विभो ।\nधृतराष्ट्रश्च कौरव्यो राजानश्च वयोऽधिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In my name, lord, you must greet her, and Dhritarashtra the Kaurava, and the older kings."}},{"n":47,"text":"भीष्मं द्रोणं कृपं चैव महाराजं च बाह्लिकम् ।\nद्रौणिं च सोमदत्तं च सर्वांश्च भरतान्पृथक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Greet Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, the great king Bahlika, Drona's son, Somadatta and all the Bharatas one by one."}},{"n":48,"text":"विदुरं च महाप्राज्ञं कुरूणां मन्त्रधारिणम् ।\nअगाधबुद्धिं धर्मज्ञं स्वजेथा मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, embrace also Vidura, of great wisdom, minister of the Kurus, of unfathomable mind and knower of dharma."}},{"n":49,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा केशवं तत्र राजमध्ये युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअनुज्ञातो निववृते कृष्णं कृत्वा प्रदक्षिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to Keshava in the midst of the kings, Yudhishthira, with leave, turned back after circling Krishna."}},{"n":50,"text":"व्रजन्नेव तु बीभत्सुः सखायं पुरुषर्षभम् ।\nअब्रवीत्परवीरघ्नं दाशार्हमपराजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But as he went, Bibhatsu spoke to his friend, best of men, the unconquered Dasharha, slayer of enemy heroes."}},{"n":51,"text":"यदस्माकं विभो वृत्तं पुरा वै मन्त्रनिश्चये ।\nअर्धराज्यस्य गोविन्द विदितं सर्वराजसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Govinda, what was agreed among us before in our counsel, half the kingdom, is known to all the kings."}},{"n":52,"text":"तच्चेद्दद्यादसङ्गेन सत्कृत्यानवमन्य च ।\nप्रियं मे स्यान्महाबाहो मुच्येरन्महतो भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, mighty-armed one, he gives that without hindrance, honoring us and not scorning us, I shall be pleased and they will be freed from great peril."}},{"n":53,"text":"अतश्चेदन्यथा कर्ता धार्तराष्ट्रोऽनुपायवित् ।\nअन्तं नूनं करिष्यामि क्षत्रियाणां जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"But if the Dhartarashtra, ignorant of the right way, acts otherwise, then I shall surely make an end of the kshatriyas, Janardana."}},{"n":54,"text":"एवमुक्ते पाण्डवेन पर्यहृष्यद्वृकोदरः ।\nमुहुर्मुहुः क्रोधवशात्प्रावेपत च पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the Pandava said this, Vrikodara was thrilled with joy, and again and again, in the grip of rage, he trembled."}},{"n":55,"text":"वेपमानश्च कौन्तेयः प्राक्रोशन्महतो रवान् ।\nधनंजयवचः श्रुत्वा हर्षोत्सिक्तमना भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trembling, the son of Kunti let out loud roars, his mind greatly elated on hearing Dhananjaya's words."}},{"n":56,"text":"तस्य तं निनदं श्रुत्वा संप्रावेपन्त धन्विनः ।\nवाहनानि च सर्वाणि शकृन्मूत्रं प्रसुस्रुवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his roar, the bowmen shook, and all the animals let fall dung and urine."}},{"n":57,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा केशवं तत्र तथा चोक्त्वा विनिश्चयम् ।\nअनुज्ञातो निववृते परिष्वज्य जनार्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thus spoken to Keshava and declared his resolve, Arjuna turned back with leave, embracing Janardana."}},{"n":58,"text":"तेषु राजसु सर्वेषु निवृत्तेषु जनार्दनः ।\nतूर्णमभ्यपतद्धृष्टः सैन्यसुग्रीववाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When all those kings had turned back, Janardana, glad, sped swiftly on with his Shaibya and Sugriva horses."}},{"n":59,"text":"ते हया वासुदेवस्य दारुकेण प्रचोदिताः ।\nपन्थानमाचेमुरिव ग्रसमाना इवाम्बरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Driven by Daruka, Vasudeva's horses seemed to drink the road and swallow the sky."}},{"n":60,"text":"अथापश्यन्महाबाहुरृषीनध्वनि केशवः ।\nब्राह्म्या श्रिया दीप्यमानान्स्थितानुभयतः पथि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty-armed Keshava saw on the way sages standing on both sides of the road, shining with the glory of Brahman."}},{"n":61,"text":"सोऽवतीर्य रथात्तूर्णमभिवाद्य जनार्दनः ।\nयथावत्तानृषीन्सर्वानभ्यभाषत पूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Janardana quickly got down from the chariot, saluted them all properly, and spoke to them with honor."}},{"n":62,"text":"कच्चिल्लोकेषु कुशलं कच्चिद्धर्मः स्वनुष्ठितः ।\nब्राह्मणानां त्रयो वर्णाः कच्चित्तिष्ठन्ति शासने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is all well in the worlds? Is dharma well kept? Do the three classes remain under the rule of the brahmanas?"}},{"n":63,"text":"तेभ्यः प्रयुज्य तां पूजां प्रोवाच मधुसूदनः ।\nभगवन्तः क्व संसिद्धाः का वीथी भवतामिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having honored them, Madhusudana said: Where, revered ones, have you achieved perfection, and what is your path here?"}},{"n":64,"text":"किं वा भगवतां कार्यमहं किं करवाणि वः ।\nकेनार्थेनोपसंप्राप्ता भगवन्तो महीतलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is the task of your reverences, and what shall I do for you? For what purpose have you come to the surface of the earth?"}},{"n":65,"text":"तमब्रवीज्जामदग्न्य उपेत्य मधुसूदनम् ।\nपरिष्वज्य च गोविन्दं पुरा सुचरिते सखा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jamadagni's son Parashurama, an old friend of one who had done well, embraced Govinda and answered Madhusudana."}},{"n":66,"text":"देवर्षयः पुण्यकृतो ब्राह्मणाश्च बहुश्रुताः ।\nराजर्षयश्च दाशार्ह मानयन्तस्तपस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Divine seers, doers of merit, learned brahmanas and royal seers, Dasharha, honoring austerity,"}},{"n":67,"text":"देवासुरस्य द्रष्टारः पुराणस्य महाद्युते ।\nसमेतं पार्थिवं क्षत्रं दिदृक्षन्तश्च सर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"who have seen the ancient war of gods and asuras, radiant one, and who wished to see the assembled kings and warriors from everywhere,"}},{"n":68,"text":"सभासदश्च राजानस्त्वां च सत्यं जनार्दन ।\nएतन्महत्प्रेक्षणीयं द्रष्टुं गच्छाम केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"and the kings in the council, and you, Janardana, in truth: this great spectacle we go to see, Keshava."}},{"n":69,"text":"धर्मार्थसहिता वाचः श्रोतुमिच्छाम माधव ।\nत्वयोच्यमानाः कुरुषु राजमध्ये परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"We wish to hear words of dharma and profit from you, Madhava, spoken among the Kurus in the midst of the king's court, scorcher of foes."}},{"n":70,"text":"भीष्मद्रोणादयश्चैव विदुरश्च महामतिः ।\nत्वं च यादवशार्दूल सभायां वै समेष्यथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, Drona and the others, and Vidura of great wisdom, and you, tiger of the Yadavas, will meet in the assembly."}},{"n":71,"text":"तव वाक्यानि दिव्यानि तत्र तेषां च माधव ।\nश्रोतुमिच्छाम गोविन्द सत्यानि च शुभानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"We wish to hear there your divine speech and theirs, Madhava, Govinda, true and good."}},{"n":72,"text":"आपृष्टोऽसि महाबाहो पुनर्द्रक्ष्यामहे वयम् ।\nयाह्यविघ्नेन वै वीर द्रक्ष्यामस्त्वां सभागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have our leave, mighty-armed one; we shall see you again. Go without hindrance, hero; we shall see you in the assembly."}}]}]}